Argyle is a tall man in [[Org/Iconoclasm/index|Iconoclasm]] who smells of frankincense and myrrh, wears armor, and carries a shield. He is a trained healer, and is a contact of [[Org/The Scale/People/Dame Quay|Dame Quay]] in [[Org/The Scale/index|the Scale]]. His grandmother heads the Scale's arbiters, and his family are reformists, who would use whatever tools come to hand; they stand against the Puritans of Custode [[Org/The Scale/People/Macarius Vesper|Macarius Vesper]], the Scale's second in command. He talks like an officer of the Scale, asks to be called Dr. Argyle, FFCS, apprentice timekeeper, and holds that hiding is a form of lying.

He was killed in the attack on the [[Org/Roundhat Gang/index|Roundhat Gang]] at [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Sableclutch/The Crowded Flea|the Crowded Flea]], and his soul did not return with the others; the Party dreamed of it chained between a light pulling up and a dark pulling down.

Argyle came back from the dead. He says the [[Divinity/Outer Gods/Judge of Ages|Judge]] ripped him from perdition and set him back in the same body, a little taller and with different eyes, his raiment twice the size it had been. The body he wears is a demon-spawn's, a grandson of the Judge whom a squad of Judge recruits once pulled out of a fortress in a Joker world. The one who wears it is a celestial who served the Judge and was bound to the demon-spawn when the demon-spawn was a child, a punishment for a failure he no longer remembers and a second chance. The demon-spawn went voidward, and Argyle means to bring him back. He calls the demon-spawn the other half, says the two were bonded and are meant to be bonded, and does not mean to kill him. [[Divinity/Fiends/Flintlock Toboggan|Flintlock Toboggan]] is the demon-spawn's uncle. [[Org/The Scale/People/Dame Quay|Dame Quay]] expects him to find the other half on the coming [[Phenomena/Pilgrimage|pilgrimage]], and says the old binding ritual will not serve because the two separated on bad terms. Anyone who sees another Argyle should tell him at once, since it is likely a demon wearing his face.

The [[People/Sharp the Cunning Man|Cunning Man]] checked him and found no demon or devil in him, and he rejoined the others at the [[Sin and Tonic]]. He now gives free medicine to people who cannot pay, working as a back-alley surgeon, and keeps his money in small jewels rather than trust the money system. He broke the curse laid on [[Org/The Scale/People/Lance Vesper|Lance Vesper]] by a coven of nighthags, which drained the man's life to feed their own, after eight hours of ritual; Lance gave him a pin of the Scale bearing his order's crest. He has also grown curious about the history of the [[Org/Iridescent Church/index|Iridescent Church]] and the cycle of Aurelia's rebirth, without meaning to convert.

He shares leadership of the Party with [[People/Anzu|Anzu]] since its founder [[Org/Iconoclasm/People/Illmari Vaino|Illmari]] went missing. When the Party entered [[People/Egan Arithmites|Egan]]'s mind to study the [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Herald|Herald]] song's hold there, it was Argyle who freed him, reaching into his soul and burning the dark out of it. He does not trust Egan, calling him the opposite of everything he believes.
